  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ7698008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**2026-09-08: slug-anchor convention prototyped**",
    "text": "**2026-09-08: slug-anchor convention prototyped**: slug-anchor authoring convention (`slugify()`-derived, `/`-joined segment paths as explicit `<a name>` anchors, referenced via plain `#fragment` links) prototyped and validated live in `test-slugifed-path.md`, as a more compact, pre-ingestion-friendly alternative to hand-typing the full-heading-text `[[deep-path]]` form, e.g.:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ7698003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D8P0009",
      "BlockNode:00CDC0D8P000A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ769800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**2026-09-09: `kg:title` removal**",
    "text": "**2026-09-09: `kg:title` removal**: Slice 1's lead-in-term extraction (`astParser.ts`'s `extractLeadInTitle`) made a pre-existing title mechanism, `kg:title` (an out-of-band, graph-only title override, decoupled from a block's own text), impractical by comparison: `reconcile.ts`'s `carryForwardFields` only ever carried a title forward when the block's *text* matched exactly, so a manually-set title was silently lost on the very next edit to that text — a real, if long-standing, fragility surfaced only once a real alternative (a title derived deterministically from the text itself) existed to compare it against. Removed `kg:title` outright (`kgTitle.ts`, its two service ops, `carryForwardFields`'s title line) in favor of the explicit lead-in term as the one and only title mechanism, for every block type. `kg:update` (`kgUpdate.ts`) gained a compensating capability: a heading target's title, being the one block type actually projected back to disk, is now itself editable by piping a leading heading line whose `#` depth matches the target's own (rejected otherwise) — mirroring exactly how a real document's heading is parsed (anchor-stripped, tree-anchor prop carried through). Fixed one adjacent, pre-existing bug found while wiring that path: `kg:update`'s default (non `--text-only`) reconcile branch never included `props` in its own reconcile shape at all, so any heading update through it — title-changing or not — silently dropped that heading's tree-anchor prop; it now defaults to preserving the target's existing props unless the new heading-rename path explicitly supplies a replacement.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ7698003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ769800C",
