    "title": "**2026-09-10: lead-in colon end-of-run fix**",
    "text": "**2026-09-10: lead-in colon end-of-run fix**: Live re-ingestion of this concern's own Slice 2 draft (`planning/linking.md`) surfaced a bug in `findLeadInColonOffset`'s (`astParser.ts`) space-after-colon check: a lead-in colon that's the very last character of its own mdast text node (e.g. `- **Heading**:` immediately followed only by nested list children, no inline \"rest\" on the same line) always fell through as if genuinely ambiguous, because the check read the next character from that text node's own truncated `.value` rather than the real document — there was nothing left to find, not because anything suspicious followed. Fixed by treating \"nothing left in this text run\" the same as \"a space follows\"; the earlier guards (inline-code exclusion, bold/italic exclusion) run first and are unaffected. See [Design](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4TG000) and [Discussion](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ76TR00E).",
