  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Motivation: dogfooding vs. shipping**",
    "text": "**Motivation: dogfooding vs. shipping**: Every `kg:*` command today is its own `tsx`-run entrypoint (`web/src/lib/kgX.ts`) invoked as `npm run kg:X -- <args>` — that only works inside a source checkout of this repo, with `tsx` and every other devDependency installed. That's fine for us dogfooding the skills we write against this CLI, but the skills under `skills/` are meant for end users, who won't have this repo cloned. Before more skills lean on `kg:*` commands, the CLI itself needs to be something installable and runnable standalone.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G007:links:Link:00CF11BFZG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G007:links:Link:00CF11BFZG000:props:StringProp:00CF11BFZG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "357"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Considered: one bin per verb**",
    "text": "**Considered: one bin per verb**: Register each existing `kgX.ts` as its own `bin` entry (`aperas-ingest`, `aperas-tree`, ...). Minimal code change — every file already runs standalone. Rejected: pollutes the user's PATH with roughly twenty near-identically-named commands, and throws away the single `aperas <verb>` entrypoint every illustrative example in the corpus already assumes (e.g. [design/documentation.md's Crystallization step](../design/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CDD68E8800B): `echo \"...\" | aperas update design/crud.md/Architecture`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Landing on: one dispatcher binary**",
    "text": "**Landing on: one dispatcher binary**: A single `aperas` executable that argv-dispatches to a subcommand (`aperas ingest ...`, `aperas tree ...`, ...). Low-risk refactor: every `kgX.ts` already separates a pure `run*` function (e.g. `runIngest`, `runProject`) from its own `main()`'s argv-parsing/help-printing glue — the dispatcher only needs to own argv routing and reuse the existing `run*`/`request()` calls and `kgHelp.ts` machinery, not rewrite any command's logic.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**the runtime**",
    "text": "**the runtime**: `tsx` (on-the-fly TypeScript execution) is a devDependency today, not something to ship a published CLI depending on. Needs a real build step (`esbuild`/`tsc`) compiling to plain JS, with `bin` pointing at the built entrypoint (a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang) — `npm run kg:X` during development can keep using `tsx` unchanged; only the published artifact needs to be compiled.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDDVC33G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**where's the graph?**",
    "text": "**where's the graph?**: `getArtifactsDir()` resolves `AperasKG/artifacts` as a hardcoded sibling of `web/` — true for us, not for an end user with no such sibling folder. Packaging needs some answer for where an installed `aperas` binary finds (or creates) its own graph — cwd-relative discovery, an env var, a config file — that's still open, and probably the biggest remaining unknown, separate from the dispatcher/bundling mechanics above.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
