  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGAFQR0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The pieces needed were already in `node.ts`, just private to `ingestFromDisk`",
    "text": "The pieces needed were already in `node.ts`, just private to `ingestFromDisk`: `collectLinkTargetsByBlock`/`collectOldWikilinksByBlock` snapshot a block's pre-mutation resolved link state, and `extractLinkCodes` (`artifacts.ts`) reads the `linkCodes` a fresh parse already stashes per node. Both are now exported, plus a new `findEnclosingArtifactId` (mirroring `artifactPathOfBlock`'s walk, but returning an id) so a command that starts from an arbitrary Block/ArtifactNode target — not `ingestArtifact`'s own already-known artifact id — can still find the right node for `resolveBlockLinks`'s `danglingRef` bookkeeping.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGAFQQR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGAFQR0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`kg:update`",
    "text": "`kg:update`: the old-link snapshot is taken right after `oldShape` (before any mutation); whichever branch (`--text-only` or the default reconcile) builds the new tree also now extracts pending link codes from it *before* hydrating — same order `ingestFromDisk` uses, since `extractLinkCodes` strips the schema-unknown `linkCodes` field as it walks. `kg:insert`'s create mode does the same over its freshly-parsed `topLevel`, with empty old-state maps (nothing existed before).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGAFQQR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGAFQR0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Verified two ways",
    "text": "Verified two ways: a throwaway `kg:insert`'d block with a `#id/...` link resolved immediately (`kg:backlinks` showed the new block as a real backlink, not just a reported count); and a no-op `kg:update` reconcile of an existing two-link block reused both `Link` ids rather than minting duplicates (`kg:backlinks` afterward showed the same two entries, unchanged).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGAFQQR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved: heading retitle-in-place, at the reconcile level too**",
    "text": "**Resolved: heading retitle-in-place, at the reconcile level too**: `kg:update`'s direct-heading-retitle feature only ever covered *targeting the heading itself*; a whole-document/whole-tree push (targeting the ArtifactNode, or a real `kg:ingest` re-parse of an edited file) still went through `reconcile.ts`'s generic `diffChildren`, where a heading's Stage A match key is `title` alone (`leafKey`) — an edited title was an exact-key miss with nothing to fall back on, so the entire subtree beneath a retitled heading reconciled as wholesale removed+added, exactly what happened above.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R002",
      "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Added a Stage A2 to `diffChildren`",
    "text": "Added a Stage A2 to `diffChildren`: headings still unmatched after Stage A's exact-title pass get a positional fallback — bucketed by depth (`astParser.ts`'s new `headingDepth`, reading the title's own leading `#` run, so a `##` can never fool-match a `#`), then paired in original relative order within each bucket. Same \"position is the anchor\" trade-off Stage B already accepts for `list`/`listItem` containers, just extended to headings once title itself is off the table as a key. A pair matched this way (or via Stage A's own text-only case) that differs in `title` and/or `text` is counted as `changed`, not folded into `matched` (`headingChanged`, generalized from the old `headingTextChanged`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Verified on a throwaway test artifact",
    "text": "Verified on a throwaway test artifact: retitling its H1 through a whole-document `kg:update` (the same shape of push that caused the original incident) now reports \"2 matched, 1 changed, 0 added, 0 removed\" — the two section headings matched cleanly, the retitled H1 counted as changed, and disk projection confirmed all three BlockNode ids were preserved (no tombstones).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGGTE6R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGN9FMR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved: the `cli-packaging.md` → `packaging.md` rename itself**",
    "text": "**Resolved: the `cli-packaging.md` → `packaging.md` rename itself**: Redone now that both blockers above are fixed. Sequence used, per doc: (1) retitle the H1 directly (`kg:update --text-only` targeting the heading BlockNode itself, not the ArtifactNode) — confirmed first that none of the five H1s carried their own `.text`/`.props`, so `--text-only`'s unconditional overwrite of those fields on a heading-target update was a no-op, not a loss; (2) fix each internal cross-reference bullet's own path text (`cli-packaging.md` → `packaging.md`) via `kg:update` targeting that specific leaf block directly, one at a time — not a whole-document push, so Stage A's ordinary exact-key matching (unaffected by the title/path edits happening elsewhere in the same document) is what reconciles each one, with nothing at stake beyond that one block's own identity; (3) `git mv` each file, then scoped `kg:ingest --track --flush`, one concern at a time.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CDGN9FMR002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDGN9FMR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Verified past the summary line",
    "text": "Verified past the summary line: every renamed ArtifactNode still carries its original id (`00CDDTBJBG000`/`00CDDTBQWG000`/`00CDDTBYG0000`/`00CDDTC3S0000`/`00CDDTC8H0000`), none tombstoned, and no orphaned `cli-packaging.md`-pathed entry survives. A couple of the cross-reference bullets (the ones with no bold lead-in term, so no rendered id-anchor — e.g. the Dashboard list) had never actually had their `[[wikilink]]`s resolved at all before this pass, since they were authored before the `kg:update`/`kg:insert` link-resolution fix above existed; fixing their path text was incidentally also the first time they got resolved.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDGN9FMR001",
