  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDWB1Y6R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**a real gap — no raw single-node inspection command**",
    "text": "**a real gap — no raw single-node inspection command**: Noticed while investigating: reaching for a Python one-liner against `BlockNode.jsonld` directly, rather than any `kg:*`/`aperas` command, to check a node's exact `.text`/`.props`/`.tombstonedAt`/`.path`. Not because list/heading structure is opaque to `kg:tree` — it isn't, given enough `--depth` it shows every list/listItem id, falling back to the bare id as its own label when there's no title. The actual gap: `kg:tree`/`kg:backlinks --text` only ever show a *rendered preview* (title + truncated, anchor-stripped abstract) — the right thing for browsing, but not for verifying a stored field is exactly what's about to be pushed back, or reading a field `kg:tree` never shows at all (`props`, `tombstonedAt`). `kg:project --dry-run` reconstructs real markdown but only at the whole-artifact level, anchors included. No command exists for \"dump this one node's raw stored state, untransformed.\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
