        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8005",
    "text": "The skill was factored out of `kg-doc-ingest` once a second workflow needed the same practices, and grew from there by accretion — one item per live incident, appended in the order things were learned.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8006:links:Link:00CF49M7F0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE95MVP8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8006:links:Link:00CF49M7F0000:props:StringProp:00CF49M7F0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "72"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8006",
    "text": "Its full text was dumped verbatim into this concern's discussion doc as [v0 SKILL.md (verbatim, 2026-09-12)](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CE95MVP8001), split so that every item is an individually addressable block, making the rewrite discussable by citation rather than by line number.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The governing philosophy was stated explicitly for the first time",
    "text": "The governing philosophy was restated in the graph itself for the first time — the ApeironNgn-era corpus had been operating on it without ever naming it, which is why the skill's most load-bearing statement had ended up last in a flat list. It is not new: `archive/Aperas-design.md` has carried it from the start, as the Apeiron/Aperas/Peras triad, the fluid-core-versus-crystallized-interface split, and deep read/deep write as the Multi-Agent Projection Pattern's defining capabilities. That founding document is itself written as an unbounded tree of nested list items with no headings at all — practising the Freeflow shape the skill only later stated as a rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8008:links:Link:00CF4A6KPG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE9FTDAR004",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8008:links:Link:00CF4A6KPG000:props:StringProp:00CF4A6KPR000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "166"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5MHD8008",
    "text": "A gap between documented practice and normative design was found and closed in the same pass: the Freeflow-as-unbounded-tree rule existed only in the skill, never in [`design/documentation.md`'s own Scratchpad section](../design/documentation.md#id/BlockNode:00CE9FTDAR004), which still showed a heading-based example. Folded back into the design doc.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
