    ],
    "title": "00CF2MWE68000",
    "text": "**The skill states the citation-direction constraint but never the obligation that follows from it**: because an `issues` block may not cite a `discussion` block, a finding promoted up out of discussion can only be linked from its origin — the discussion entry has to gain the forward link at the moment of promotion. Nothing in the skill says so. Citation direction states what is forbidden and stops; *Discussion is where meta-info is born* argues the opposite caution, against promoting prematurely, which primes hesitation before filing rather than care once filing is legitimate; *Dense linking is the precondition* states the principle with no trigger attached to it. The passage that would name the missing step — [Crystallization — content and topology](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG00J), whose topology axis is exactly this lifecycle — exists only in the design doc and was never carried into the operational skill file by the v1 restructure. Confirmed live: seven issues filed into a new concern from findings recorded across four discussion docs, every origin left unlinked, invisible from the new doc's own side and caught only by direct user callout. **Resolved**: the skill gained a `### Promotion links at the origin` section under Discipline, directly after Citation direction — stating that the link is added at the origin pointing up, that it happens at the moment of promotion rather than as a later tidying pass, and naming crystallization's topology axis with a pointer to the design doc rather than importing it wholesale.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
