      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF5ZK3ZG002:props:StringProp:00CF5ZK5Q8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CF5ZK3ZG002",
    "text": "**Its companion** — [a look-it-up rule is only half a discipline](#id/BlockNode:00CF5ZE1S0003) — grounds why the read-side instruction was declined rather than added. Doing the work and recording the work are two separate acts here, and only a comparison against the world outside the graph can see the second one missing. That principle is what the drift check implements.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF5ZK3ZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF5ZK3ZG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CF5ZK3ZG003",
    "text": "**Both zeroes were found forward**, from the realizer's empty grounding, where \"keep an active view\" was found backward from the principle's empty backlinks. Two directions, two defect shapes, one walk — and the second one was only available because a one-directional query had already been caught being one-directional.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF5ZK3ZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
