      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF5ZS9QR001:props:StringProp:00CF5ZSBCG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CF5ZS9QR001",
    "text": "**v1.2 — the recall machinery got the principle that makes it non-optional, and the tooling prompted its own recording for the first time**: snapshot, delta, drift check and the `Supersedes` marker had all been built without anything above them explaining why they are required rather than convenient — a forward audit of [the thread](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CF4D9XT0001) returned zero grounding for each. Closed by a Philosophy statement that *nobody working this graph will remember, so the graph must be what notices*, with its companion explaining why a look-it-up rule is only half a discipline: doing the work and recording it are separate acts, and only a comparison against the world outside the graph can see the second one missing. Recorded as [the v1.2 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CF5ZE1S0001). Notable for how the recording happened: `scripts/skill_drift.py` reported all three additions the moment they were written, so for the first time the record was prompted by the tooling rather than by a reader noticing an omission — which is the principle demonstrating itself within minutes of being stated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF6AJYP0001",
