    "title": "**Same shape as the write-side gap, one step earlier**",
    "text": "**Same shape as the write-side gap, one step earlier**: [Philosophy's \"a look-it-up rule is only half a discipline\"](#id/BlockNode:00CF5ZE1S0003) diagnosed why a *stated* instruction doesn't self-execute on the write side. This is the identical failure on the read side, one level further out — before a rule can be half a discipline, something has to load the rule in the first place, and nothing here does that mechanically.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF6R1KP8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF6R1KP8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Two candidate fixes, not mutually exclusive, neither built yet**",
    "text": "**Two candidate fixes, not mutually exclusive, neither built yet**: broaden the description to name source-code investigation/editing explicitly (cheap, but soft — the same shape of fix a stated-condition list already is, just a longer list); or a mechanical trigger outside the skill file entirely — a hook firing on a Read/Edit/Grep touching `monorepo/**`, unbidden, the same category of fix `skill_drift.py` already is for the write side. Which to build is not yet decided.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF6R1KP8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
