    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80MKFR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v1.3** — v1 restructured a flat, incident-ordered list of eighteen items into four levels, abstract to concrete; the arrangement was the defect. v1.1 repaired the vertical thread between those levels: crystallization stated at Philosophy and Orientation rather than only as a Discipline rule, and dense linking realized below Orientation rather than only asserted there. v1.2 grounds the recall machinery — snapshot, delta, drift check — in the Philosophy statement that makes it non-optional. v1.3 replaces a mechanical read-side gate, found fragile in three ways during testing, with a one-time consent question the skill asks and remembers instead of enforces, and rewrites the description in plain terms, scoped to the whole session rather than to graph edits alone. Concern docs: `AperasKG/artifacts/{design,issues,planning,history,discussion}/aperas-skill.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80MKFR001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001:props:StringProp:00CF80TX68000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001:props:StringProp:00CF80TX68001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CF80TVJG001",
    "text": "**A mechanical read-side gate was built, tested, and broke three separate ways — none of them a config typo**: to close the trigger gap just above, a `PreToolUse` hook (`skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py`) was registered in a personal `.claude/settings.local.json` — deliberately never shared, since a hard gate baked into the project would be the \"destroys the whole meaning of skill\" mistake the entry above warns against. It denied `Read`/`Edit`/`Grep` under `monorepo/packages/**` and `AperasKG/**` until the session had run a real `aperas` command, tracked by a session-scoped marker file. Two rounds of live testing found three independent bugs, each confirmed rather than guessed at.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG002",
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR000",
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR001",
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR002",
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR003",
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG002:props:StringProp:00CF80TX68002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG002:props:StringProp:00CF80TX68003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Bug 1 — the Bash trigger matched the project's own name**",
    "text": "**Bug 1 — the Bash trigger matched the project's own name**: `Bash(*aperas*)` was meant to open the gate on a real `aperas` invocation, but the repository itself is named `Aperas`, so any `find`/`ls`/`grep` command that merely touches a path under it also matches. Confirmed by the marker file's own mtime landing 3–4 seconds after a session's very first `find` call — long before any `Read` of graph content, let alone a real orientation. Fixed by anchoring to the actual invocation shape, `Bash(npm run aperas -- *)`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Bug 2 — the gated path was never the path actually used**",
    "text": "**Bug 2 — the gated path was never the path actually used**: `AperasKG` is a symlink whose real target, `/home/will/source/AperasKG`, sits *outside* the project root as a sibling, not nested under it. A relative `if` pattern resolves against `<cwd>/AperasKG/**`, but every real `Read` call resolved through the symlink and used the target path directly — a different absolute path that pattern can never match. The rule was dead the day it was written; confirmed by running the identical `Read` through both path forms under `--debug hooks` and watching one skip and the other fire. Fixed with an absolute-anchored `//`-pattern naming the real location, kept alongside the harmless, still-inert relative one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Bug 3 — a stale decoy sat at an ungated path**",
    "text": "**Bug 3 — a stale decoy sat at an ungated path**: `skills/aperas-workspace/kg-clone/` — a disposable, gitignored eval-sandbox clone of the whole graph, reproducible via `graph-sandbox.sh` — held copies of the same filenames at a path neither rule covered, so an agent exploring with `find`/`ls` could wander in and read from there with none of the gate's discipline attached. It was not even current: it predated this session's own `cli.md`/`core.md` split. Removed outright.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What actually found these — not reasoning about VS Code, a real headless run with hook tracing**",
    "text": "**What actually found these — not reasoning about VS Code, a real headless run with hook tracing**: `claude -p \"<prompt>\" --debug hooks --debug-file <path>` runs one real session and logs every hook match, skip, and the exact JSON decision returned. Guessing at Bug 2 by reasoning about the VS Code extension's process lifecycle produced a plausible but wrong diagnosis (a stale-process theory, \"restart VS Code\" — which changed nothing); the debug trace found the actual cause in one run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The example that was tested, kept here since the file itself doesn't survive**",
    "text": "**The example that was tested, kept here since the file itself doesn't survive**: `.claude/settings.local.json` is personal and gitignored by design, so this is its only durable record.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CF80TVJR004",
    "text": "```json\n    {\n      \"hooks\": {\n        \"PreToolUse\": [\n          {\n            \"matcher\": \"Read\",\n            \"hooks\": [\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Read(monorepo/packages/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" },\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Read(AperasKG/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" },\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Read(//home/will/source/AperasKG/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" }\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"matcher\": \"Edit\",\n            \"hooks\": [\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Edit(monorepo/packages/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" },\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Edit(AperasKG/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" },\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Edit(//home/will/source/AperasKG/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" }\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"matcher\": \"Grep\",\n            \"hooks\": [\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Grep(monorepo/packages/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" },\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Grep(AperasKG/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" },\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Grep(//home/will/source/AperasKG/**)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py\" }\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"matcher\": \"Bash\",\n            \"hooks\": [\n              { \"type\": \"command\", \"if\": \"Bash(npm run aperas -- *)\", \"command\": \"python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/skills/aperas/scripts/aperas_gate.py --mark\" }\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n    ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR003",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CF80TVJR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
