    "title": "The document's own past stays out",
    "text": "The document's own past stays out: prior wordings, a section's retired name, tool behaviour that has since changed, and version history all belong in `discussion/aperas-skill.md`. This is distinct from [the originating incident above](#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG00B), which is provenance rather than history — it explains why a rule that is true now is true, and so travels with the rule. The test is whether a sentence still reads to someone with no memory of the version that preceded it, and a correction appended to text left unfixed always fails it. That is why the repair is to rewrite the item until it is complete on its own, never to leave it standing and add a paragraph explaining what the earlier one got wrong.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG00A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
