          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`aperas update` never re-derives a non-heading block's title**",
    "text": "**`aperas update` never re-derives a non-heading block's title**: Found live [while rewriting Topology for the skill's v2](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CGF35FNG001): `aperas update` replaced a paragraph's `.text` correctly and left `.title` frozen at the value ingest had derived, so the node went on rendering under a title stating the very rule its new text had just retired. Re-running the update with a deliberately short lead-in term, well inside `extractLeadInTitle`'s heuristics, changed nothing; an `insert` of a sibling paragraph minutes later derived its title from the lead-in correctly, so the defect is in `update`'s path rather than in parsing. Promoted to [issues/linking.md's Open Issues](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGFE4SV0002).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ37GPRR009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G002",
      "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G003",
      "BlockNode:00CGGA9J68000",
      "BlockNode:00CGGA9J68001",
      "BlockNode:00CGGA9J68002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G002:links:Link:00CGF83G90002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CDBZ769800B",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G002:links:Link:00CGF83G90002:props:StringProp:00CGF83G90003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CGF83D4G002",
    "text": "[The `kg:title` removal](../history/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBZ769800B) left the lead-in term as the one and only title mechanism for every block type, and gave `kg:update` a compensating path for heading targets only — a heading being the one block type whose title is projected back to disk. That reasoning holds for the projection: the paragraph's rendered markdown is correct and the stale title is invisible on disk. It does not hold for the graph, where `tree`, `unfold` and `backlinks --text` all display the title and nothing marks it stale, so the block reads as saying one thing in preview and another in full.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGF83D4G003",
    "text": "`reconcile.ts`'s `carryForwardFields` carries a title forward only when the block's text matches exactly, which should have left a changed paragraph with no title rather than the old one — so this is likely `update`'s own field handling, not the reconcile rule. The summary line reports `0 changed` and says nothing about the title either way, which is the usual silent shape. Not yet traced to the specific call, and there is no CLI route to repair an already-stale title short of tombstoning the block.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGF83D4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGFE4SV0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
