    ],
    "title": "**Graph-wide sweep for the pre-fix \"wikilink never resolved\" residue — 9 real cases found and fixed, not the 20 first estimated**",
    "text": "**Graph-wide sweep for the pre-fix \"wikilink never resolved\" residue — 9 real cases found and fixed, not the 20 first estimated**: `resolveBlockLinks` used to run only from `kg:ingest`, never `kg:update`/`kg:insest` ([this doc's own account above](#id/BlockNode:00CF1276D0001)) — already fixed in the current code, but every node last touched before that fix kept a permanently-empty `.links` regardless of what its text actually cited. A first pass (any stored `text` containing `](...#...)`with an empty `.links`) found 20 candidates graph-wide; most turned out to be false positives once checked by hand — a fenced code-block example in `design/documentation.md` with placeholder ids (`00C0000000001`, all zeros), and half a dozen copies of `SKILL.md`'s own wikilink-syntax documentation quoting the pattern with a literal `<ID>`/`...` placeholder inside backticks, none of them real citations at all. Re-run comparing each node's *actual* `#id/BlockNode:...` fragments (code fences and inline-code spans excluded from the count) against its resolved `.links` targets found exactly 9 genuine cases, spread across `planning/linking.md`, `issues/packaging.md`, `history/aperas-skill.md` and `discussion/aperas-skill.md` — all resolvable (every target confirmed live, none tombstoned or missing). Fixed by re-touching each with `aperas update <id> --text-only` (piping the node's own unchanged text) — chosen over a plain `update` specifically because a plain reconcile risks tombstoning real children on a node whose full shape isn't known up front (the near-miss recorded just above this entry); `--text-only` never reconciles children at all, so it was safe regardless. Confirmed by re-running the same precise sweep afterward: zero remaining. A companion check for the opposite failure — a resolved `Link` whose *target* is now dead or missing — also came back empty, so this concern's link integrity is otherwise clean as of this pass.",
