    "title": "**Tier 2 — hides Tier-1-style problems, or blocks legitimate writes outright**",
    "text": "**Tier 2 — hides Tier-1-style problems, or blocks legitimate writes outright**: [a props-only change reports as `0 changed`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CFATMWY0001) — cheap to fix, and fixing it makes every other write's verification trustworthy, which every other item on this list depends on. [`extractAnchorNames` treats a backtick-quoted example anchor as a real claimed name](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGGHVBF8001) — the opposite failure mode from the rest of this tier: a false collision that *blocks* a legitimate `insert`/`resolve` rather than corrupting data, but still a direct edit-path stoppage.",
