    ],
    "title": "00CGMVKQM0001",
    "text": "[x] Investigated and fixed. Verified against `issues/packaging.md`'s own dead nested-list-wrapper chain by direct reproduction: a childless-of-its-own `listItem` wrapping a nested one-item list, with the nested item removed via `aperas remove` — the wrapper stayed `!tombstonedAt` indefinitely, since `pruneUnreachableTombstones`'s mark phase walks structurally reachable nodes regardless of tombstone status (it never needed to prune it) and nothing else ever revisited a live container's own liveness once its children changed. Fixed with a new companion sweep, `tombstoneVacuousContainers`, run at the same three explicit-sweep call sites as `pruneUnreachableTombstones` (`reloadStore`, `clobberFlush`, shutdown): marks `tombstonedAt` on a `list` node with no live children, or a `listItem` with no text of its own and no live children, repeating to a fixed point so tombstoning an inner wrapper can vacate its own parent in turn — [issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG006).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGK3AH60001",
