    "title": "**Follow-up, on review**",
    "text": "**Follow-up, on review**: the 40-discrepancy sweep above was real and its own match logic worked correctly for it, but only because every code in this corpus embeds the target's opaque id as a literal substring (`path#id/<ID>`, `aperas://id/<ID>`) — the check compared `code`/`target.id` by raw containment, which cannot verify `[[<deep-path>]]` addressing (`resolve.ts`'s deep-path grammar, a real, currently-live convention per `history/linking.md`, not covered by any of the 40). Fixed in [issues/linking.md](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGN6GJVG000) by resolving each occurrence for real instead of guessing from the string.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX88R0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
