  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CHXVRBT0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T09:13:03.887Z",
    "title": "00CHXVRBT0002",
    "text": "`0740b04` (\"Guard frontmatter of skills with `>-`\") reformatted the YAML `description` into a folded block scalar for parser safety, without ever re-recording the new shape here — `skill_drift.py` flagged it as \"ADDED but unrecorded\" ever since. Same words, new shape, quoted verbatim below:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CHXVP090001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CHXVRBT0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CHXVRBT0003",
    "text": "```\n---\nname: aperas\ndescription: >-\n  Before anything else in this project — first turn, every session, whatever the task looks like,\n  including when it looks unrelated, trivial, read-only, or like one quick lookup — check memory\n  for a standing decision on whether Aperas manages this session. Do this without loading this\n  skill, and never ask permission to do it or offer it as an option; just do it. If a decision\n  is recorded, follow it. If none is, ask with AskUserQuestion using exactly these choices —\n  Never / Not now / Yes, this session only / Yes, all sessions — and record only 'all sessions'\n  or 'never' durably, so a session-scoped answer is asked again next session. Load this skill\n  only once the answer is yes; it then governs the work — orient in the graph before acting,\n  change it through the CLI rather than by editing files, put back what the work turns up.\n  Aperas is this project's external memory: a knowledge graph, worked through the `aperas` CLI,\n  holding what has been decided, tried, found and planned. For first-time ingest of existing\n  documents, `kg-doc-ingest` covers that; this one first.\n---\n\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CHXVP090001",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
