    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-17T20:06:34.275Z",
    "title": "**2026-09-18: Slice 1 landed — `buildRenderTree` in core**",
    "text": "**2026-09-18: Slice 1 landed — `buildRenderTree` in core**: `discoverCone`'s render plan is now returned as a structured `RenderItem` tree (`buildRenderTree`, `@aperas/core`) instead of being flattened straight to strings; `renderTreeWithView` is now `toText(buildRenderTree(...))`, and the `tree` service op takes a `format` discriminator — `'render-tree'` returns the structured tree (requires `--view`; the structured render only exists for the view-based renderer), omitted or `'text'` keeps the string-lines shape. Verified byte-identical against the pre-refactor renderer on a real, richly-unfolded corpus view (preview/expanded/pointer link modes, tombstone tagging, fold counts all covered) alongside the existing `verify`/`verify:slow` suites, both still clean.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6N9R003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
