    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ83NV3G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**2026-09-18: a real dev build, clicked through end to end**",
    "text": "**2026-09-18: a real dev build, clicked through end to end**: `packages/web` renders the live corpus via a Solid `FolderDiv`, driven entirely by real graph state through a dev-only bridge to the ApeironNgn service (talking to it directly over its unix socket — the same `request`/`ensureServiceRunning` every `kg*.ts` entrypoint already uses — rather than shelling out a CLI subcommand per click, which the first version of this bridge did and which made fold/unfold feel like seconds-per-click; a `flush: true` inherited from that first version separately forced a full content-mirror dehydrate on every fold/unfold too, since `service.ts`'s own cases set the content-dirty flag unconditionally). Working end to end and confirmed against the live graph, not just the UI: fold/unfold writes to the real `TreeView.unfolds` set; ctrl-click zoom and breadcrumbs change apex; prose is rendered as real markdown with navigable inline links (resolved via the same `#id/<Kind>:<snowflake>` anchors design/linking.md already writes); a hover popover previews a link's target and can promote it into `unfolds`; the edit pencil is Slice 8's shallow write, piping straight to `aperas update --text-only` and verified round-tripping type/parent/children unchanged.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6N9R003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
