    "title": "**A bare relative-path link (no fragment) never resolved at all**",
    "text": "**A bare relative-path link (no fragment) never resolved at all**: `astParser.ts`'s `collectLinkCodes` only ever extracted a link occurrence in three shapes — `[[code]]`-wrapped, `aperas://` scheme, or anything containing a `#` — so an ordinary `[title](../folder/file)` reference with no fragment was invisible to resolution entirely, not merely dangling: confirmed live on an existing corpus link with zero entries in its own `.links`. [Topology](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007) already described this form as valid (\"cross-file navigation... an ordinary relative path\"), just never implemented. **Fixed**: `collectLinkCodes` now also extracts a `./`/`../`-leading href with no fragment; `apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`'s `resolveOneCode` routes it through a new `resolveBarePathCode`, canonicalizing via the same OS-relative arithmetic the fragment form already uses (`leadingPart.ts`) and resolving directly to whatever's live there — no anchor-matching gate needed, since a bare path names exactly one target. Documented as its own addressing form in [Projected/Pre-Ingestion Context](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C). Corpus-wide `check-links --repair` found and fixed 2 more pre-existing instances of the same gap once the resolver landed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
